## Python pipeline example
This example loads objects and search from the Metropolitan Museum of Art API into DuckDB. It mirrors the endpoint and data selector configuration from the table above:
```  
import dlt  
from dlt.sources.rest_api import RESTAPIConfig, rest_api_resources

@dlt.source  
def metropolitan_museum_of_art_source():  
    config: RESTAPIConfig = {  
        "client": {  
            "base_url": "https://collectionapi.metmuseum.org/public/collection/v1",  
        },  
        "resources": [  
            {"name": "objects", "endpoint": {"path": "public/collection/v1/objects", "data_selector": "objectIDs"}},  
            {"name": "departments", "endpoint": {"path": "public/collection/v1/departments", "data_selector": "departments"}}  
        ],  
    }  
    yield from rest_api_resources(config)

def get_data() -> None:  
    pipeline = dlt.pipeline(  
        pipeline_name="metropolitan_museum_of_art_pipeline",  
        destination="duckdb",  
        dataset_name="metropolitan_museum_of_art_data",  
    )  
    load_info = pipeline.run(metropolitan_museum_of_art_source())  
    print(load_info)  
```
To add more endpoints, append entries from the resource table to the `"resources"` list using the same `name`, `path`, and `data_selector` pattern.
